      "title": "Psi-expansion conjecture for interval graphs",
      "canonical_url": "https://mathdb.com/p/360770/psi-expansion-conjecture-for-interval-graphs",
      "literal_statement": "Let $G=([n],E)$ be an interval graph. For a composition $\\alpha\\vDash n$, let $\\Psi_\\alpha$ be the type 1 power sum quasisymmetric function, let $z_\\alpha=z_{\\lambda(\\alpha)}$, and let $\\mathcal{N}_{G,\\alpha}$ be the set of permutations defined by requiring that each segment of composition shape $\\alpha$ has neither a $G$-descent nor a nontrivial left-to-right $G$-maximum. Let $\\omega$ be the involution on $\\operatorname{QSym}$. **First conjecture.**\n\n$$\n\\omega \\chi_G[X;q]=\\sum_{\\alpha\\vDash n}\\frac{\\Psi_\\alpha}{z_{\\alpha}}\\sum_{\\sigma \\in \\mathcal{N}_{G,\\alpha}}q^{\\widetilde{\\mathsf{inv}}_G(\\sigma)}.\n$$\n\nThis extends the power-sum expansion known for Dyck graphs and proposes a quasisymmetric analogue for interval graphs.",
