      "canonical_url": "https://mathdb.com/p/361269/impropriety-bound-for-2-trees",
      "literal_statement": "Let $G$ be a **2-tree**, that is, a graph obtained from a triangle by repeatedly adding a new vertex adjacent to both endpoints of an existing edge. Let $\\mu_{\\operatorname{int}}(G)$ denote the impropriety of an interval coloring of $G$. **2-tree impropriety conjecture.**\n\n$$\n\\mu_{\\operatorname{int}}(G)\\leq 2.\n$$\n\nThe conjecture is motivated by the fact that the smallest 2-tree, $K_3$, has impropriety $2$, while the source reports no 2-tree with larger impropriety. Its status is unresolved in the supplied text.",
